From bd2b2efed0f9d0823f03d45069789fdc6b0bfea9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: n0madic <800462+n0madic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:01:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: SMAA on the picture, the default anti-aliasing

FXAA blends across every edge it finds, which dims the short horizontal
strokes of small text. SMAA 1x (preset HIGH) finds the shape of each edge
and leaves straight edges and one-pixel lines alone. It is built from the
reference SMAA.hlsl and the precomputed area and search textures in the
paraLLEl-GS checkout's Granite (MIT); the shader is embedded by CMake.
PS2_HOST_AA selects smaa (default), fxaa or off; SMAA falls back to FXAA
when it is not built in or does not compile.

Both filters now take their texture coordinate from the output pixel, so
their render textures keep the picture's row order and SMAA's passes read
each other the same way up. The intermediate passes draw without alpha
blending, since the edges and weights carry data in their alpha channel.
---
